-- Second round of real-OSM-geometry upgrades: segments that were true
-- no_match in the original pipeline pass, re-queried with a wider bbox and
-- looser endpoint tolerance. Each accepted match was checked against known
-- real-world elevations for its named landmarks before being applied here,
-- to guard against the wrong-branch mismatches this pipeline is prone to at
-- trail junctions (see the POI-matching incident from the prior session).
-- Two rejected candidates from this same retry pass are NOT included:
--  * Bearpaw Meadow -> Hamilton Lake matched, but its endpoint elevation
--    (2819m) is ~300m above Hamilton Lake's real elevation (~2510m) --
--    almost certainly overshot past the lake, further up the switchbacks
--    toward Precipice Lake on the same named way.
--  * Horseshoe Lake -> Snag Lake matched via a 3-way chain but missed its
--    target endpoint by 1.4km -- too large an error, on a multi-junction
--    chain, to trust without a stronger independent check.

